LICENCE: NOT YET DETERMINED
===========================

**This repository has no licence yet, and that is on purpose. Do not treat the
absence of one as permission.** Until a licence is added here, no rights are
granted: no copying, no modification, no redistribution, no use in another
project. Under default copyright law that is the position whether or not this
file says so — this file exists so that nobody has to guess.

Why it is unresolved
--------------------

This code was written by the author in the course of employment. Work made in
that context is very often owned by the employer rather than the author,
regardless of who typed it, so the author is not currently in a position to
grant anyone a licence to it. The publication of this build is a portfolio
demonstration — a scrubbed copy with a fictional company, no real data and no
internal documents — and publishing it is not a claim of ownership over it.

Resolving this means getting the employer's written position on (a) whether this
build may remain published, and (b) whether the code may be licensed for reuse,
and if so under what terms. Until that answer exists in writing, this file
should stay exactly as it is.

The realistic options, once ownership is settled
------------------------------------------------

**MIT.** The shortest permissive licence: anyone may use, modify and
redistribute the code, including commercially, provided the copyright notice and
licence text travel with it, and the software is provided without warranty.

**Apache-2.0.** Permissive on the same terms as MIT, plus an explicit patent
grant from contributors, a requirement to state significant changes, and clearer
handling of trademarks and contributions — the usual choice where a company is
the copyright holder and wants that extra certainty.

**Source-available, viewing and evaluation only.** A custom grant permitting
anyone to read the code and evaluate the author's work, while reserving every
other right — no use, no modification, no redistribution. This is the option if
the employer is content for the repository to stay public as a portfolio piece
but does not want its code reused, and it is the likeliest outcome for a
line-of-business application like this one.

Whichever is chosen, replace this entire file with the licence's exact text, add
the correct copyright line naming whoever actually owns the copyright, and say
so in the README.
